<title>USA: Alumax shares undervalued - report.</title>
<headline>Alumax shares undervalued - report.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Based on the replacement value of Alumax assets, its shares are worth over $50, said Tony Hitschler, head of Brandywine Asset Management, in Business Week.</p>
<p>Alumax rose 1/2 to 33-1/4 on the New York Stock Exchange on Thursday.</p>
<p>Hitschler thinks a large foreign metals company could soon make an attractive offer to Alumax, according to the report.</p>
<p>In February, Alumax rejected an cash and stock offer by Kaiser Aluminum Corp to buy the company for $40 to $45 a share.</p>
</text>
